# Books. Never, under any circumstance, commit these.
#
# The books live in Library/Application Support/Chartered Book, outside this
# folder, so ordinarily there is nothing here to leak. This folder may still
# hold the copy left behind when the books moved, so it is shut out by name as
# well as by pattern.
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.zip
# The finished downloads are the exception. They are what people actually
# click, so they belong in the repository. They are built by
# tools/make_release.py and checked for book files before they are written.
!download/*.zip
# The browser build carries the engine as a zip. Without it the app loads and
# then fails on unpacking, so it has to be committed like any other source.
!docs/app/*.zip
# And the downloads themselves, which are served from the site rather than
# from a folder beside it, so that the link on the install page points inside
# the domain instead of at a code host.
!docs/download/*.zip
chartered-book.log

# Anything exported or backed up
backups/
*.csv
*.xlsx

# Built things. The Mac app is made from the source by
# python3 tools/make_mac_app.py, so it does not belong in the repository.
Chartered Book.app/
dist/
build/
release/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Editors and the operating system
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
chartered_book/BUILD.txt
